                                                "sense_id": "c7ea071c-eab5-3ffd-90f0-03e5b728b2ab",
                                                "text": "Trust funds do not have to be remitted to The Bahamas and the settlor does not have to be resident or physically present in The Bahamas. However, the trustees (whether corporate or individual) should be located in The Bahamas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e4a5666-054c-4a95-9072-fe6fc17c57fe",
                                                "sense_id": "c7ea071c-eab5-3ffd-90f0-03e5b728b2ab",
                                                "text": "From The Bahamas to the U.S. and Canada, postage rates are as follows: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69c9b672-9069-485e-94ef-12b7133904a8",
                                                "sense_id": "c7ea071c-eab5-3ffd-90f0-03e5b728b2ab",
                                                "text": "A local agent for the IBC must be appointed, but company meetings may be held anywhere, while migration of IBCs to and from The Bahamas is facilitated, allowing immediate transfer of financial assets."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
